{# No <main> wrapper here: render_page already wraps every body in one with the
   same classes, and this template was the only one on the site adding a second.
   Two <main> elements is invalid HTML and leaves assistive tech without a single
   primary landmark. #}

  <section class="text-center mb-10">
    <img src="/treesmith/icon-160.png" alt="Treesmith app icon"
         width="80" height="80"
         class="block w-20 h-20 mx-auto mb-4 rounded-2xl shadow">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">
      Track the trees you buy from treestock
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-xl mx-auto mb-6">
      Treesmith is a phone app for keeping track of every tree in your
      collection. Log grafts and harvests, and add photos as they grow. It's
      made by the same person who runs treestock.
    </p>
    {# Official store badges, served locally from /treesmith/ (deploy.sh copies
       static/). Both vendors require their own supplied artwork rather than a
       lookalike button, and the badges are far more recognisable than the plain
       text buttons they replace (DAL-222). Google's PNG has clear space baked
       into the asset, so it is rendered at 60px tall to make its visible pill
       match Apple's 40px one. width/height are the display sizes so the hero
       reserves the space before the images load. #}
    <div class="flex gap-2 flex-wrap justify-center items-center">
      <a href="{{ ios_url }}" class="inline-block">
        <img src="/treesmith/app-store-badge.svg" alt="Download Treesmith on the App Store"
             width="120" height="40" class="h-10 w-auto">
      </a>
      <a href="{{ android_url }}" class="inline-block">
        <img src="/treesmith/google-play-badge.png" alt="Get Treesmith on Google Play"
             width="155" height="60" class="h-[60px] w-auto">
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-3">Free for up to 30 plants. Pro is a one-time purchase that unlocks unlimited plants.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-12">
    <div>
      <img src="/treesmith/grid.png" alt="Plant grid view in Treesmith"
           class="w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Your collection at a glance</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
        Every plant with its photos, species and variety, plus where and when
        you got it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <img src="/treesmith/detail.png" alt="Plant detail with photo timeline"
           class="w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Growth over time</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
        Photos of flowering, fruiting, new growth and harvest, each one dated
        and saved with the plant.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <img src="/treesmith/activity.png" alt="Activity log in Treesmith"
           class="w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">A full care history</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
        Log watering, pruning, feeding, repotting, harvests, pest treatments
        and grafts, so you can look back at what you've done with each tree.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-lg p-6 mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-green-900 mb-2">Why we built it</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-green-900 mb-2">
      treestock helps you find where to buy a rare variety. Treesmith helps you
      remember which one you bought, where it came from, when you grafted it,
      and how it's gone since.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-green-900">
      Sooner or later a collection outgrows a spreadsheet or the Notes app.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="grafting" class="mb-10 scroll-mt-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">If you graft</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-2">
      Graft tracking is the part Rare Fruit Club WA members asked for. Each graft
      is saved with the tree it went onto, along with the technique, the date,
      where the scion wood came from, and whether it took.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
      The Treesmith site also has a
      <a href="{{ grafting_techniques_url }}" class="underline text-green-700">guide to 19 grafting techniques</a>,
      with sources and notes on which stock and season each one suits. It's
      worth a read before your next whip-and-tongue, whether you use the app or
      not. You can also
      <a href="{{ graft_tracking_url }}" class="underline text-green-700">see how graft tracking works</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Pricing</h2>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Free</h3>
        <ul class="text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1 list-disc pl-5">
          <li>Up to 30 plants</li>
          <li>One location</li>
          <li>Photos, activity log, GPS garden map</li>
          <li>Local export</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-green-300 bg-white rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-green-900 mb-2">Pro</h3>
        <ul class="text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1 list-disc pl-5">
          <li>Unlimited plants</li>
          <li>Multiple locations</li>
          <li>Reminders and bulk operations</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-3">One-time purchase. No subscription.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-4">
      Cloud backup is a separate yearly subscription, and you need Pro first.
      It backs up every day and syncs between your devices. It's yearly because
      the servers cost money to keep running. Everything else works offline,
      and you can export your data for free on any plan.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="text-center mb-12">
    <a href="{{ app_url }}"
       class="inline-block bg-green-700 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-lg text-lg font-semibold shadow hover:bg-green-800 hover:shadow-md">
      See more at treesmith.app &rarr;
    </a>
  </section>

  {# Trademark attribution required by both vendors' badge guidelines, now that
     the hero uses their supplied artwork rather than plain text buttons. #}
  <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 text-center mb-8">
    Apple and the Apple logo are trademarks of Apple Inc., registered in the U.S.
    and other countries. App Store is a service mark of Apple Inc. Google Play and
    the Google Play logo are trademarks of Google LLC.
  </p>

